{"name":"Cornwall","hex":"#4885aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cornwall","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A peninsula, cultural area, maritime ceremonial county, and duchy in England; forming its south-western extremity, bordered by Devon in the east.","The country  of the Cornish, currently having the status of a royal duchy in England belonging to the male heir apparent to the reigning monarch, and consisting at least of the Cornwall County and the Isles of Scilly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cornwall"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cornwall","blocks":[{"text":"Cornwall is a ceremonial county in South West England. It is one of the Celtic nations and the homeland of the Cornish people. The county is bordered by the Atlantic Ocean to the north and west, Devon to the east, and the English Channel to the south. The largest urban area is the Redruth and Camborne conurbation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/St_Michael%27s_Mount_View.jpg/330px-St_Michael%27s_Mount_View.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornwall"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/The_stamps_and_whim_engine_house_at_Wheal_Coates_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1476958.jpg/330px-The_stamps_and_whim_engine_house_at_Wheal_Coates_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1476958.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/The_stamps_and_whim_engine_house_at_Wheal_Coates_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1476958.jpg/330px-The_stamps_and_whim_engine_house_at_Wheal_Coates_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1476958.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_stamps_and_whim_engine_house_at_Wheal_Coates_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1476958.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org